<title>USA: IMF to send mission to Pakistan to discuss loan.</title>
<headline>IMF to send mission to Pakistan to discuss loan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Monetary Fund has agreed to send a mission to Pakistan to negotiate a resumption of lending to the country following &quot;constructive&quot; talks between the two sides, monetary sources said Thursday.</p>
<p>The sources, who declined to be named, said the talks here centered on a package of economic measures aimed at putting Pakistan's economy back on track.</p>
<p>The IMF has withheld part of a $600 million standby loan because of concerns about Pakistan's economic performance.</p>
</text>
